#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096615 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096415 :question/id #uuid "f61ac550-d62c-558f-b6d5-0d4c9aba8089" :question/math-academy-id "e-3629" :question/problem "Given that $y=4\\log_3 x,$ find $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we apply our formula for the derivative when the base of the logarithm is a number other than $e.$ By doing so, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\t\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}&=\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(\\log_3 x\\right)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t &=4\\cdot\\dfrac{1}{x \\ln 3}\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t&=\\dfrac{4}{x \\ln 3}.\n\n}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5856f3cc-5423-5a97-b2fd-7f44e0797ec7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097018 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fc74cbb-55e3-58fe-93f7-23d2f90e74b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094082} {:answer/id #uuid "c8eb47da-1745-5e7e-9737-588db0279dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094083} {:answer/id #uuid "27f824f3-9710-5d1e-89d8-290ab212a196" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094084} {:answer/id #uuid "38a4b8f7-dd90-5e68-8316-42e512e1e894" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{1}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094085} {:answer/id #uuid "4599b2f9-9707-597b-9797-37f1b2b1555a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094086}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5630eeac-2ac2-529f-8c22-77ea989d69be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094081}] :question/id #uuid "f06ecd5e-5944-5764-a8e8-9da3fea992d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-11903" :question/problem "Given that $y = x - 3\\log_{5} x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6f74602-324e-53ca-838c-8b274a97bc96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x - \\frac{7}{x\\ln 9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094088} {:answer/id #uuid "bb439b88-d8d5-5ce1-97d2-fff353d9a6cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{x\\ln 5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094089} {:answer/id #uuid "e85a174f-b0d2-5831-bff8-3555b6382def" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x - \\frac{1}{x\\ln 9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094090} {:answer/id #uuid "16661e50-45a6-585e-90ce-2d427494b71b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{1}{x\\ln 9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094091} {:answer/id #uuid "21e9072b-91cf-598e-9f41-3597bcbc89ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x - \\frac{7}{x\\ln 9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094092}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f26be675-4841-5853-9c73-242d275f5343" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094087}] :question/id #uuid "5483eb06-46ab-500c-9fb8-8d630575623c" :question/math-academy-id "q-11907" :question/problem "Given that $y = x^{2} - 7\\log_{9} x$, find $\\frac{dy}{dx}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233051 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d746064f-9bc3-5f26-9c93-afaf01c3e7e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-101719" :question/problem "Given that $y=7-4{log}_{3}x$, find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}3}.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7-4{log}_{3}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7)-4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{3}x) \\\\  & =0-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{x\\operatorname{ln}3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1/\\operatorname{ln}3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1/\\operatorname{ln}3} & ={(-\\frac{4}{x\\operatorname{ln}3})\\,|}_{x=1/\\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7910af85-fe7d-5c72-bfa8-012147c4fad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7910af85-fe7d-5c72-bfa8-012147c4fad3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232810} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a0533ea-5c3b-54d0-8191-c267a1815911" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232809}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2dd8674-7fa4-5d68-955d-c19f5b7e1758" :question/math-academy-id "q-339989" :question/problem "Given the function $y=4{x}^{2}-6{log}_{3}x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{2}-6{log}_{3}x) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2x-6\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =8x-\\frac{6}{x\\operatorname{ln}3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(8x-\\frac{6}{x\\operatorname{ln}3})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =8(1)-\\frac{6}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}3} \\\\  & =8-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4dcaf086-29eb-58e3-9792-842c7a25fb05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dcaf086-29eb-58e3-9792-842c7a25fb05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-\\frac{3}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232812} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4aa8b73-2643-5d54-9ecf-8c68f6f1aaca" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232811}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c0ddc214-9263-5104-9473-b379b6f7ec26" :question/math-academy-id "q-339997" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={log}_{7}x-3\\operatorname{ln}x$, find ${f}^{'}(x).$\n\n${f}^{'}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{'}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{7}x-3\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{7}x)-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-3(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(7)}-\\frac{3}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241022 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0442097d-1b68-55b7-9cb8-c462931d1330" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238117} {:answer/id #uuid "0e522cac-c75a-5c1f-9bac-01ed6857debd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{ln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238178} {:answer/id #uuid "44b6755c-aead-5542-8a1b-64818f1fbff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238650} {:answer/id #uuid "461da220-919b-5435-93cc-a2ea3dad39d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238664} {:answer/id #uuid "ffca6930-a453-5efc-ba11-64e5e1be934c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0442097d-1b68-55b7-9cb8-c462931d1330" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238117} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bea711e-203a-5f4c-8d6c-0248b489ff5c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240554}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7a3193e7-39e5-59fc-a3d8-c6e491fa4479" :question/math-academy-id "q-105256" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={7}^{x}+{log}_{5}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({7}^{x}+{log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & ={7}^{x}\\cdot ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5} \\\\  & ={7}^{x}\\text{ }ln⁡7+\\frac{1}{xln⁡5}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253529 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "010fae26-d218-5d85-80be-b5da7fa03138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250562} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7274d3-9d6c-566f-8ab0-5d6dadc206db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250801} {:answer/id #uuid "3fea77d7-dd38-54a3-ab38-de4a5e6af670" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251082} {:answer/id #uuid "90d31982-431c-5c96-9fd1-28cbe6930c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251788} {:answer/id #uuid "e56177c0-fb1c-54a8-8c75-934ef63a1c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90d31982-431c-5c96-9fd1-28cbe6930c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251788} :answer-field/id #uuid "35ef16c9-7f8c-57e6-86fd-b4dbee5a6bfa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252894}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9de855f-8e10-5bff-89a6-c3649ce380b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-11900" :question/problem "Given that $y=5{log}_{4}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}⁡x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{xln⁡4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287936 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08d6c7d7-cbc8-50f3-a344-45446b405f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284858} {:answer/id #uuid "2557b0d8-9f3c-5e2b-a795-8eef0be2c846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285117} {:answer/id #uuid "265b440a-0541-5605-93d6-05c026a9c562" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285122} {:answer/id #uuid "7663eb58-65d7-5b9c-a07b-0641ecb1169d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285889} {:answer/id #uuid "eb874120-2ccd-5cec-a284-10e8ad025134" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{4}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08d6c7d7-cbc8-50f3-a344-45446b405f44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284858} :answer-field/id #uuid "2efe99a9-b212-56ab-a943-1bebc7a16391" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287245}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "884748ff-1cf0-5818-a246-3daa4fae09f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-1921" :question/problem "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ for $f(x)={2}^{x}+\\operatorname{log}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({2}^{x}+\\operatorname{log}⁡x) \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10} \\\\  & ={2}^{x}\\text{ }\\operatorname{ln}⁡2+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a21d7c1-657b-5c7c-bc8d-a5a78f0a5e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}3}-4+5e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295600}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a21d7c1-657b-5c7c-bc8d-a5a78f0a5e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}3}-4+5e" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295600} :answer-field/id #uuid "24fc67ac-4879-57d5-8bd2-d439a30262bd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296699}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8688ee43-a87d-5757-aeae-1697946d83af" :question/math-academy-id "q-308866" :question/problem "Given the function  $y=2{log}_{3}⁡x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+5{e}^{x},$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{log}_{3}⁡x-4\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+5{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{4}{x}+5{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{4}{x}+5{e}^{x})\\,|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{1\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{4}{1}+5{e}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-4+5e\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "277904a9-9e9e-53f0-a87c-616303962482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312275}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "277904a9-9e9e-53f0-a87c-616303962482" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312275} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bb11537-ff22-5776-85db-c4e4d92da407" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314045}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b9fb0b98-97be-5fa4-a0a8-73b036fd9d03" :question/math-academy-id "q-339994" :question/problem "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x,$ find the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3.$ Do not round the answer.\n\nThe instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTo find the instantaneous rate of change at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}+x-3{log}_{6}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}+1-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡6} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the instantaneous rate of change at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(6{x}^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{xln⁡6})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =6(3)^{2}+1-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot ln⁡6} \\\\  & =55-\\frac{1}{ln⁡6}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29a1b399-700a-5dd2-967b-49969d3534b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(10)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29a1b399-700a-5dd2-967b-49969d3534b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)+\\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}(10)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312291} :answer-field/id #uuid "38b53a32-4b9b-556b-afd9-471f5f44697e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314162}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6065f3ff-ff9c-5643-832d-8d1ba7e4dfa6" :question/math-academy-id "q-340105" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={3}^{x}+log⁡x$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}+log⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(log⁡x) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}ln⁡(3)+\\frac{1}{xln⁡(10)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6cea7a0d-5e57-5d82-b9dc-783b5889bf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}+\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}(5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312833}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6cea7a0d-5e57-5d82-b9dc-783b5889bf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}+\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}(5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312833} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b6adce3-ac95-53df-964b-74afaf250503" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314381}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05a9cae0-c21b-5778-9f36-154aaf19469f" :question/math-academy-id "q-340106" :question/problem "Given that $y=-{e}^{x}+3{log}_{5}⁡x$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To differentiate a logarithm with base $a,$ we use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{a}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{xln⁡a}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-{e}^{x}+3{log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{5}⁡x) \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}+3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡(5)} \\\\  & =-{e}^{x}+\\frac{3}{xln⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Logarithmic Function With a General Base"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096616 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096416 :question/id #uuid "5eaa00f8-0fd0-5de6-a7c0-965db6de3a5c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3630" :question/problem "Given that $y= \\log_4 x + \\ln x$,  find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left( \\log_4 x + \\ln x \\right)\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\log_4 x) + \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}(\\ln x )\\\n\t\t&= \\dfrac{1}{x\\ln 4} + \\dfrac{1}{x}.\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{1}{xln⁡4}+\\frac{1}{x})|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{ln⁡4}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cef7fc21-23f4-5d6a-a208-9963ef23c784" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050711 :topic/math-academy-id 332 :topic/title "Calculating the Slope of a Tangent Line Using Differentiation"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097136 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a1ef8d-83de-5766-9657-a3bfe0bb38dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094790} {:answer/id #uuid "0252fcd7-aeab-5761-8acd-d83247a91140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094791} {:answer/id #uuid "0ec8a347-f04f-5b31-b96a-f6161c05a063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094792} {:answer/id #uuid "3d77c43e-3716-58ad-bfa3-1b5969543ef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094793} {:answer/id #uuid "6a1e92d9-bcf0-58ec-9823-44766ae56d64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094794}] :answer-field/id #uuid "7f1d45b3-2a55-54df-9843-cd54e2302ddb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094789}] :question/id #uuid "0259cf05-81de-512b-a7bb-bd7b4b70d4e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-17373" :question/problem "Given that $y =-\\frac{3}{5}\\ln x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x = 1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097137 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c9535bbe-8473-5599-9eae-86f82aec85f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094796} {:answer/id #uuid "f914470b-dc52-52fd-977b-65814c410cbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln 3 + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094797} {:answer/id #uuid "3208ddc6-452f-5f4f-bfef-252a124463b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094798} {:answer/id #uuid "45323c64-e7df-59cc-84f6-49f89ffab9e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{\\ln 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094799} {:answer/id #uuid "70fe78d5-79ed-559e-ab74-f865abba7a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\ln 3} + 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094800}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6bb3288b-51b9-54b1-8b95-4333cd4a102b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094795}] :question/id #uuid "55e0676e-8226-56ea-844c-41bb8f4c2189" :question/math-academy-id "q-17395" :question/problem "Given that $y = \\log_{3} x + 5\\ln x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x = 1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233052 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ae057d0-d78b-5718-aa6f-daab4feb4650" :question/math-academy-id "q-101723" :question/problem "Given that $y=4{e}^{x}-3{log}_{7}x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}7}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope  of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}7})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{3}{3\\operatorname{ln}7} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}7}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c8b4247-2f6e-5c89-84d3-05e82fd928d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c8b4247-2f6e-5c89-84d3-05e82fd928d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232814} :answer-field/id #uuid "b23a283b-6469-55b9-90b7-faa54b42b98a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232813}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "203042d7-3a90-5b98-a3a8-41d259d10f67" :question/math-academy-id "q-340014" :question/problem "Given the function $y=5{x}^{2}+6\\operatorname{ln}x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=3$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5{x}^{2}+6\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x) \\\\  & =5\\cdot 2x+6\\cdot \\frac{1}{x} \\\\  & =10x+\\frac{6}{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(10x+\\frac{6}{x})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =10\\cdot 3+\\frac{6}{3} \\\\  & =32\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233903 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe3da45a-b176-52b2-a1fc-b27d861de6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}-18\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232816}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe3da45a-b176-52b2-a1fc-b27d861de6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}-18\\operatorname{ln}3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232816} :answer-field/id #uuid "263e1f60-7948-5f00-a01d-0963d8a18442" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232815}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7cc61275-8b03-5f03-bb68-53ecece9ebf0" :question/math-academy-id "q-340022" :question/problem "Given the function $y=5\\operatorname{ln}x-2\\cdot {3}^{x},$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5\\operatorname{ln}x-2\\cdot {3}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{ln}x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({3}^{x}) \\\\  & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}-2\\cdot {3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}3 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{5}{x}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{x})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}3\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}-18\\operatorname{ln}3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233905 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a68429f7-6205-5d83-9b54-817cfb429a93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232820} {:answer/id #uuid "6c1498cc-e778-47a5-bb1a-c239ac9e2a39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3e^2+\\frac{1}{\\ln4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a68429f7-6205-5d83-9b54-817cfb429a93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232820} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb82ad2c-5850-514d-a61d-c6dc21f1e26a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232819}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25397da2-818c-507a-82b9-e23dda017608" :question/math-academy-id "q-340109" :question/problem "Given the function $y=-3{e}^{x}+2{log}_{4}x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{e}^{x}+2{log}_{4}x) \\\\  & =-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{4}x) \\\\  & =-3{e}^{x}+2\\cdot \\frac{1}{x\\operatorname{ln}4} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(-3{e}^{x}+\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}4})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{2}{2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}4} \\\\  & =-3{e}^{2}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}4}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234289 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e390b863-0cc7-5db5-bfcb-f1828e76e02e" :question/math-academy-id "q-70897" :question/problem "Given that $y=2{log}_{2}x+{2}^{x}$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=2.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}2\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}2)|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{2\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}2}+{2}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}2 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}2}+4\\operatorname{ln}2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "472e11dd-8537-5b30-ad11-59c4c14c5212" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236273} {:answer/id #uuid "6d4f0ac8-1dab-5270-b011-493f700ff938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+8ln⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236509} {:answer/id #uuid "78e82567-e2b5-51dd-885b-f1af7319339c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236577} {:answer/id #uuid "90cac687-dd21-570e-a62a-f9e1d628421a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8ln⁡2-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236739} {:answer/id #uuid "97421f7d-e972-5d83-b422-5d436b8e6feb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78e82567-e2b5-51dd-885b-f1af7319339c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236577} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e2000d3-5ddf-572d-be68-d0feed75463e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237519}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "09ca9b0e-b19f-5aca-b14f-466e3c4366f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-101726" :question/problem "Given that $y=3x-5+8{log}_{2}⁡x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x-5+8{log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-5)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(8{log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5)+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =3-0+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{8}{xln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1/ln⁡2} & ={(3+\\frac{8}{xln⁡2})|}_{x=1/ln⁡2} \\\\  & =3+\\frac{8}{(\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}\\cdot ln⁡2)} \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ea60620-2ab9-5040-8270-703c9a1d6b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281818} {:answer/id #uuid "7936ae4e-f008-5af5-820c-1674250b0ac2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282726} {:answer/id #uuid "7c387048-20f2-5147-a642-ff8e502ef022" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282760} {:answer/id #uuid "90f5b318-f4a9-5268-90ba-ba237d66d663" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282944} {:answer/id #uuid "9a3d6901-3436-54f0-a0b1-ce4e806a253f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ea60620-2ab9-5040-8270-703c9a1d6b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281818} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec15cdba-b1f7-5ecd-9880-c9e9cda591f8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284349}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9bd05e5a-ceb5-5b6d-a1ee-24c21df80b24" :question/math-academy-id "q-17371" :question/problem "Given that $y=3ln⁡x+2{x}^{2}-5x$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3ln⁡x+2{x}^{2}-5x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3ln⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(ln⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{2})-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}+4x-5 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{x}+4x-5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{3}{x}+4x-5)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{1}+4\\cdot 1-5 \\\\  & =3+4-5 \\\\  & =2\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42c897e4-b652-55dd-8d72-bc5035453929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-\\frac{5}{2\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42c897e4-b652-55dd-8d72-bc5035453929" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24-\\frac{5}{2\\operatorname{ln}3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312506} :answer-field/id #uuid "32f3d565-6897-5bcf-9632-a037dba3624d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314146}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1eb887e7-89db-539c-9d35-d652e9bb15c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-340024" :question/problem "Given the function $y=2{x}^{3}-5{log}_{3}⁡x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=2$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-5{log}_{3}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})-5\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{3}⁡x) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3{x}^{2}-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡3} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{xln⁡3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=2$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=2} & ={(6{x}^{2}-\\frac{5}{xln⁡3})|}_{x=2} \\\\  & =6(2)^{2}-\\frac{5}{2ln⁡3} \\\\  & =24-\\frac{5}{2ln⁡3}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "101f0087-1aec-50e5-a9b7-d806a0ea860a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "101f0087-1aec-50e5-a9b7-d806a0ea860a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312090} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a7fc2dd-1d62-5a23-a97f-19baf25d47a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314431}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b69d4c2-7ebc-59ed-aa14-566d23bb3592" :question/math-academy-id "q-340026" :question/problem "Given the function $y=6{log}_{2}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-3x,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=1$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6{log}_{2}⁡x+4{x}^{2}-3x) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x)+4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =6\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2}+4\\cdot 2x-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{xln⁡2}+8x-3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=1} & ={(\\frac{6}{xln⁡2}+8x-3)|}_{x=1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{1\\cdot ln⁡2}+8(1)-3 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{ln⁡2}+5\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60475637-df2c-5099-a5a7-9cd23687c0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60475637-df2c-5099-a5a7-9cd23687c0fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312747} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bd5a890-600f-5ed0-9892-4e5fc04515a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314310}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5c352abb-1992-52cb-94e7-b48e48f5bbc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-340110" :question/problem "Given the function $y=4{e}^{x}-3{log}_{2}⁡x+7,$ the slope of the tangent line at $x=3$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{e}^{x}-3{log}_{2}⁡x+7) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({e}^{x})-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({log}_{2}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(7) \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{xln⁡2}+0 \\\\  & =4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{xln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=3$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(4{e}^{x}-\\frac{3}{xln⁡2})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{3}{3\\cdot ln⁡2} \\\\  & =4{e}^{3}-\\frac{1}{ln⁡2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403412 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c631962-dd2a-53db-b827-84d94e8f7e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403414} {:answer/id #uuid "8f33e14e-f91d-5c5f-9b34-7c61ede2d34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403415} {:answer/id #uuid "33140677-5da7-59ef-8215-135fba67dffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403416} {:answer/id #uuid "7fefc24f-ce9e-58b5-aba2-9f2cb372222e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403417} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3a5a72-8cb5-5f5c-812b-2114a27a36be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403418}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8f33e14e-f91d-5c5f-9b34-7c61ede2d34c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403415} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fcab4c2-5aab-5cee-8699-609d2431de61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403413}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ddfac57c-89c4-597b-b080-b0ac4a48d4c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-70903" :question/problem "Given that $y=3\\operatorname{log}⁡x+{x}^{3}-4$, find the slope of the tangent at $x=3.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the slope of the tangent at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nTaking the derivative, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+3{x}^{2}\\,.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent at $x=1$ is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{x=3} & ={(\\frac{3}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+3{x}^{2})|}_{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+3\\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡10}+27\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent Line of a Logarithmic Function at a Point"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096617 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096417 :question/id #uuid "d7a77a89-0535-54da-a246-36ee5b4e9e7f" :question/math-academy-id "e-3634" :question/problem "Differentiate $x\\cos x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\cos x .$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t (x\\cos x)' &=   u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t\t&= (x)'\\cdot \\cos x + x\\cdot (\\cos x)'\\\n\t\t\t\t\t   & = 1 \\cdot \\cos x + x (-\\sin x)\\\n\t\t\t\t\t  & =  \\cos x - x \\sin x\t\t\t\t\t\n\n}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b194bf2f-feaa-5656-a3ee-0ff466a39e77" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048593 :topic/math-academy-id 35 :topic/title "The Power Rule for Differentiation"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050420 :topic/math-academy-id 280 :topic/title "Differentiating Trigonometric Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aca48a7b-5c44-5ceb-9f7a-46475643a906" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}\\cos x - x^{2}\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094898} {:answer/id #uuid "bb75f041-eacc-5451-b3bf-166b8949e018" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\cos x - 2x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094899} {:answer/id #uuid "be19c12b-7932-58a0-8911-03fae070336e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\cos x - x^{2}\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094900} {:answer/id #uuid "01d55ed0-9518-50b6-bd31-eee6e6062db5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2}\\cos x - 2x\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094901} {:answer/id #uuid "7c36000d-a170-5e76-a4c2-7f56fa11b4fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\cos x + x^{2}\\sin x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094902}] :answer-field/id #uuid "176e6625-97a1-5955-aa6f-db131e85d138" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186094897}] :question/id #uuid "637cc150-7613-534a-bd8b-a83dc2342647" :question/math-academy-id "q-1907" :question/problem "Differentiate $x^{2}\\cos x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097244 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9123bd43-0985-5815-be98-b4a9d900c88c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x + x^{2}\\sec x\\tan x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095389} {:answer/id #uuid "c878d6c7-8a8f-5afe-acd0-f6083b75b15d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\tan x(2x + \\sec x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095390} {:answer/id #uuid "cafc2f88-c0bc-5677-aebd-e70ab8b877b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\sec x\\tan x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095391} {:answer/id #uuid "098c202e-114f-59ad-a524-c2dbaf56709e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(2\\tan x + x\\sec^{2} x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095392} {:answer/id #uuid "72022765-1175-5b0d-bf32-d2786a419e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sec x(2 + x^{2}\\tan x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095393}] :answer-field/id #uuid "634e8d5c-10ef-5420-b752-d09396e5a6f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095388}] :question/id #uuid "af8066b5-6cf6-5662-aded-c14a5c3d72ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-47965" :question/problem "Differentiate $x^{2}\\tan x$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d88db36a-1743-57b4-81de-ba3e94f146e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232540}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d88db36a-1743-57b4-81de-ba3e94f146e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232540} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cf0faa2-183e-595b-9158-aab3d3891b84" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232539}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a902a53e-f058-534a-bee4-004868eb968b" :question/math-academy-id "q-310188" :question/problem "Differentiate ${3}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}(x).$\n\n$({3}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}(x))^{'}=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,{3}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={3}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({3}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}(x))^{'} & ={u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x) \\\\  & =({3}^{x})^{'}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}(x)+{3}^{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}(x))^{'} \\\\  & =({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3))(\\operatorname{sin}(x))+({3}^{x})(\\operatorname{cos}(x)) \\\\  & ={3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}(3)\\operatorname{sin}(x)+{3}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233808 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "131acbe9-558d-5eca-b043-6011320bbf1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{tan}(x)-2)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232577}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "131acbe9-558d-5eca-b043-6011320bbf1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\operatorname{tan}(x)-2)\\operatorname{sin}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232577} :answer-field/id #uuid "db20f675-f846-587b-8b98-472e5b4e4ce4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232576}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04a32680-52e9-52f1-b831-14d1889bed06" :question/math-academy-id "q-319402" :question/problem "Differentiate $(2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))\\operatorname{cos}(x)$\n\n$((2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))\\operatorname{cos}(x))^{'}=-{sec}^{2}(x)\\operatorname{cos}(x)\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=2-\\operatorname{tan}(x)$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cos}(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}((2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))\\operatorname{cos}(x))^{'} & ={u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x) \\\\  & =(2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))^{'}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}(x)+(2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}(x))^{'} \\\\  & =(-{sec}^{2}(x))(\\operatorname{cos}(x))+(2-\\operatorname{tan}(x))(-\\operatorname{sin}(x)) \\\\  & =-{sec}^{2}(x)\\operatorname{cos}(x)+(\\operatorname{tan}(x)-2)\\operatorname{sin}(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234296 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2b5dea81-9340-51d4-993f-9f9ce501ae79" :question/math-academy-id "q-71004" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x)^{'} & ={u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{'}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (\\operatorname{sin}x)^{'} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(\\operatorname{sin}x)+({e}^{x})(\\operatorname{cos}x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}x+{e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}x\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20897b11-31f3-5236-8344-066364ab30aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238339} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9dc0f2-2211-5b4e-a2e7-26a81ec7f21c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}cos⁡x+sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238465} {:answer/id #uuid "528c811e-a747-5b55-b5c7-a2d707220097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238765} {:answer/id #uuid "c9cd3281-ae65-5560-8442-2a603e50ff12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{x}cos⁡x+sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239827} {:answer/id #uuid "cce47b31-03c3-57e4-ae08-02ac34ba2a0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}cos⁡x+{e}^{x}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "528c811e-a747-5b55-b5c7-a2d707220097" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238765} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe0d6216-93d3-5d7b-aefb-cbdf2e8a0a46" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240776}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d7240cf-a773-5ae8-8c7e-03955317789e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104297" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}cos⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=cos⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}cos⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot cos⁡x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (cos⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(cos⁡x)+({e}^{x})(-sin⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}cos⁡x-{e}^{x}sin⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "329a0351-2458-5dc2-afb3-fb83d076e70a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}sec⁡x+{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285251} {:answer/id #uuid "3d41ba8e-fd4a-5c5b-8e2c-3eb30e482c53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285366} {:answer/id #uuid "5b2ff268-76d1-583f-9abe-62b917b9c7eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{csc}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285621} {:answer/id #uuid "93783351-25ff-5c87-8ae9-958c98c327e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286129} {:answer/id #uuid "eb7d1570-7a65-5731-b765-bf52675c003d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286945}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb7d1570-7a65-5731-b765-bf52675c003d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286945} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44b9e2e-ea9e-5094-bc4f-bc781e7df5d9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287478}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a541e9ea-7fd8-5568-9e5c-f9ef03f5eaf6" :question/math-academy-id "q-1931" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}tan⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=tan⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}tan⁡x)^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot tan⁡x+{e}^{x}\\cdot (tan⁡x)^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(tan⁡x)+({e}^{x})({sec}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & ={e}^{x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+{e}^{x}tan⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299745 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bac31f3f-82dd-5744-9c52-62141c569e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+\\operatorname{sin}(x)){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bac31f3f-82dd-5744-9c52-62141c569e1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2+\\operatorname{sin}(x)){e}^{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298365} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d13588f-071e-5a52-a869-877b2c497c93" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298845}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c9a55990-04ba-5f4c-bd0b-a335f0aeb15a" :question/math-academy-id "q-319350" :question/problem "Differentiate ${e}^{x}(2+sin⁡(x)).$\n\n$({e}^{x}(2+sin⁡(x)))^{′}=$\n{{field-1}} $+\\,{e}^{x}cos⁡(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=2+sin⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({e}^{x}sec⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({e}^{x})^{′}\\cdot (2+sin⁡(x))+{e}^{x}\\cdot (2+sin⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =({e}^{x})(2+sin⁡(x))+({e}^{x})(cos⁡(x)) \\\\  & =(2+sin⁡(x)){e}^{x}+{e}^{x}cos⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299746 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70915bcc-86df-54d2-a4fe-50e0b9f25633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70915bcc-86df-54d2-a4fe-50e0b9f25633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x\\operatorname{cos}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298034} :answer-field/id #uuid "75c11172-6006-5675-abeb-a1bc58910b0a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299035}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dca45644-472a-517e-a9dd-987f8f5907bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-319357" :question/problem "Differentiate $2{x}^{2}cos⁡(x).$\n\n$(2{x}^{2}cos⁡(x))^{′}=$\n{{field-1}} $-\\,2{x}^{2}sin⁡(x)$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=2{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=cos⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{x}^{2}cos⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})^{′}\\cdot cos⁡(x)+2{x}^{2}\\cdot (cos⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =(4x)(cos⁡(x))+(2{x}^{2})(-sin⁡(x)) \\\\  & =4xcos⁡(x)-2{x}^{2}sin⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299752 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "284d504d-e400-57ba-866e-f8dff66216fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297724}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "284d504d-e400-57ba-866e-f8dff66216fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297724} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecb4d22f-ab7d-5aa3-8db2-cf3a5509f8ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299438}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9df2a3ce-ad57-5588-83d2-42b69ca3314d" :question/math-academy-id "q-319385" :question/problem "Differentiate $\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x).$\n\n$(\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x))^{′}=\\frac{tan⁡(x)}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,+$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of the two functions $u(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $v(x)=tan⁡(x).$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\sqrt{x}tan⁡(x))^{′} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{x})^{′}\\cdot tan⁡(x)+\\sqrt{x}\\cdot (tan⁡(x))^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}}(tan⁡(x))+(\\sqrt{x})({sec}^{2}⁡(x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{tan⁡(x)}{2\\sqrt{x}}+\\sqrt{x}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating a Product Containing a Trigonometric Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096618 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096418 :question/id #uuid "6bb0eded-7277-5ab5-8c13-bfc480403b1a" :question/math-academy-id "e-3635" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=x^2\\ln x,$ find $f'(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and $v(x)=\\ln x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}ln⁡x+{x}^{2}{(ln⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot ln⁡x+{x}^{2}(\\frac{1}{x}) \\\\  & =2xln⁡x+x \\\\  & =x(2ln⁡x+1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f15a60dd-f6a7-577d-bdbc-148032de94c8" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048749 :topic/math-academy-id 1114 :topic/title "Differentiating Exponential Functions"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050690 :topic/math-academy-id 1116 :topic/title "Differentiating Logarithmic Functions"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097162 :question/